# Git workflow — origin/main

When the user asks to fix, add, update, or implement anything in this repository:

1. Implement the code changes fully.
2. Commit with a clear, concise message (why over what).
3. Push directly to `origin/main` without waiting for a separate "please commit/push" request.
4. Request smart-mode approval when needed for protected `origin/main` pushes.
5. On Windows PowerShell, quote paths with parentheses and avoid bash HEREDOC; use PowerShell-safe commit message syntax.

Do not leave completed implementation uncommitted/unpushed unless the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push.
